WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.155
Plumfield School, dedicated to the memory of Elizabeth March, opened its doors three months later.

2
00:00:07.156 --> 00:00:14.513
People came from town and from neighboring cities near and far to satisfy their curiosity about the new establishment.

3
00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:24.141
"It’s a nice turnout, isn’t it?" Mr. Laurence said proudly as he waved at a few familiar faces and warmly greeted those he didn’t know as well.

4
00:00:24.142 --> 00:00:31.334
Mother kept wiping tears from her eyes as she said over and over again, "Beth would be so happy."

5
00:00:31.335 --> 00:00:40.233
Jo, along with Amy and Laurie, happily served drinks and snacks to the visitors and directed all those who had questions to Professor Bauer.

6
00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:47.460
Meg gave tours of the place while John minded the children and made sure they didn’t eat more cookies than they should.

7
00:00:47.461 --> 00:00:55.413
"I desperately need a cold drink," the Professor gasped as he politely detached himself from a group of mothers

8
00:00:55.414 --> 00:00:59.473
who had gathered to pepper him with questions about the school curriculum.

9
00:00:59.474 --> 00:01:05.495
Handing him a tall glass of lemonade, Jo asked, "Do you think it’s going to be a success?"

10
00:01:05.496 --> 00:01:11.158
Looking at her tenderly, the Professor remarked, "Jo, whatever you do will succeed.

11
00:01:11.159 --> 00:01:17.873
Do you know why?" Without waiting for an answer, he replied, "Because you put your whole soul into it."

12
00:01:17.874 --> 00:01:24.708
Laurie and Amy exchanged knowing glances as they predicted another wedding in the March family soon.

13
00:01:24.709 --> 00:01:30.470
At present, however, the Professor’s very words, like a prophecy, were about to come true.

14
00:01:30.471 --> 00:01:36.296
A young delivery boy ran up to the refreshment table asking for Josephine March.

15
00:01:36.297 --> 00:01:38.623
"That’s me," she replied.

16
00:01:38.624 --> 00:01:42.999
"Package for you, ma’am," the boy said, handing her a thick envelope.

17
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.426
"What is it, Jo?" Amy asked curiously.

18
00:01:46.427 --> 00:01:50.770
"I don’t know," Jo said as she ripped the envelope open.

19
00:01:50.771 --> 00:02:00.283
Inside was a bound book, and when Jo saw the title and author’s name, she let out a cry, "It’s my novel!"

20
00:02:00.284 --> 00:02:05.913
The Professor caught her arm to steady her while Amy took the book from Jo’s hands.

21
00:02:05.914 --> 00:02:11.776
"The Little Women: A Story About Life, by Jo March," she read.

22
00:02:11.777 --> 00:02:16.555
"Jo! This is your book! Your book’s been published!"

23
00:02:16.556 --> 00:02:23.131
Hearing Amy’s excited voice and Laurie’s cheers, Meg came running, followed by their parents.

24
00:02:23.132 --> 00:02:28.803
When Laurie held up the book, everyone clapped and shouted their congratulations loudly.

25
00:02:28.804 --> 00:02:32.915
"See, Jo, another success," whispered the Professor.

26
00:02:32.916 --> 00:02:37.446
"Your soul is in that book, just as it is in this school."

27
00:02:37.447 --> 00:02:43.460
Jo took his hand without saying a word, because he already knew what she wanted to say.

28
00:02:43.461 --> 00:02:49.169
The grand opening of the school Academy brought greater results than anyone had

29
00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:55.766
thought. It was obvious that the upcoming days would be busy with accepting applications and planning

30
00:02:55.767 --> 00:03:00.259
lessons. John quit his job and took on a position as an English

31
00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:06.694
teacher. Amy volunteered to work part-time as the art instructor, and Meg said she would teach a sewing

32
00:03:06.695 --> 00:03:15.393
class. Aside from the other teachers who were hired, Plumfield School was the joint effort of the March, Laurence, and Brookes families uniting as

33
00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:21.764
one. As she pondered that, Jo decided it would be a good chance for her to spend some private time with her

34
00:03:21.765 --> 00:03:26.435
sisters. They agreed to take a walk together, just the three of them, down to the

35
00:03:26.436 --> 00:03:33.244
pond. "This has really been an eventful day," Meg said when they reached the pond and sat on a fallen

36
00:03:33.245 --> 00:03:37.610
log. "My legs are killing me," said Amy, rubbing her sore

37
00:03:37.611 --> 00:03:42.508
feet. "But I’d gladly stand for weeks if it means making this school a

38
00:03:42.509 --> 00:03:48.921
success." The girls sat together watching a few ducks swim around the pond as the sun was sinking in the

39
00:03:48.922 --> 00:03:55.408
sky. "We used to come out here a lot when we were younger, but I haven’t been for so long," said

40
00:03:55.409 --> 00:04:02.367
Meg. "Remember how we used to swim in the water, and Jo would grab our legs and try to pull us under?" giggled

41
00:04:02.368 --> 00:04:08.208
Amy. "Then you’d run home and tell Mother or Father what I did and get me in trouble," Jo pointed

42
00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:13.545
out. "We were so young and carefree," Amy said with a smile on her

43
00:04:13.546 --> 00:04:20.182
face. "That’s why we did so many foolish things," Meg said, blushing at the memory of some of her embarrassing

44
00:04:20.183 --> 00:04:25.486
moments. "But look at us now, girls," said Jo. "Meg is a mother with two

45
00:04:25.487 --> 00:04:29.597
children. Amy is married to Laurie and may soon start a family of her

46
00:04:29.598 --> 00:04:36.898
own." "And Jo is an accomplished writer and headmistress of the most prestigious school in America," Amy added with

47
00:04:36.899 --> 00:04:41.538
pride. "By the way, you never told us what your book is about, Jo," said

48
00:04:41.539 --> 00:04:46.494
Meg. Looking out at the pond, Jo took a moment to gather her thoughts before

49
00:04:46.495 --> 00:04:52.850
answering, "It’s about dreams and failures, growing up and growing pains, love and

50
00:04:52.851 --> 00:04:59.771
heartache, opportunities and memories, regrets and hope, birth and death . . . It’s about

51
00:04:59.772 --> 00:05:05.534
life." The sisters grew silent as they watched the sun slowly disappear below the

52
00:05:05.535 --> 00:05:11.632
horizon. "I miss her so much," Amy said, choking up as her mind filled with memories of

53
00:05:11.633 --> 00:05:18.184
Beth. As they used to do when they were younger, the girls wrapped their arms around each other and

54
00:05:18.185 --> 00:05:22.717
cried. "Beth wouldn’t want us to cry every time we think of her," sniffed

55
00:05:22.718 --> 00:05:25.687
Amy. "You’re right," Meg said, wiping her

56
00:05:25.688 --> 00:05:30.995
eyes. "Beth was always a positive, happy girl, and that’s how I want to remember

57
00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:37.926
her." "Remember how she used to always get excited whenever we started a new chapter in a book?" asked

58
00:05:37.927 --> 00:05:45.847
Jo. Giggling at the memory, Amy said, "She said new chapters are the best because there is so much to look forward

59
00:05:45.848 --> 00:05:50.853
to." Jo dried her eyes and looked at her sisters. "What do you say,

60
00:05:50.854 --> 00:05:56.772
girls? Let’s tell each other about the new chapters in our lives that are about to begin," she

61
00:05:56.773 --> 00:06:03.476
suggested. Meg started first. "My new chapter begins with Daisy and Demi starting

62
00:06:03.477 --> 00:06:11.492
school. While they learn how to become good citizens, I will learn how to be a better mother, wife, daughter, and

63
00:06:11.493 --> 00:06:18.714
sister." "My new chapter begins with finding a house for me and Laurie to live in," said Amy, and laughed along with her

64
00:06:18.715 --> 00:06:24.388
sisters. "Then each day I want to do something that will touch the life of another person in some

65
00:06:24.389 --> 00:06:30.843
way, whether through my words, actions, instructions as a teacher, or even through my

66
00:06:30.844 --> 00:06:40.689
paintings." Finally it was Jo’s turn. "My new chapter begins with the start of a new outlook on life, on relationships, on goals, and on

67
00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:47.797
myself. I hope to treasure each moment as it deserves to be valued and love each person as they deserve to be

68
00:06:47.798 --> 00:06:56.589
loved." Hugging each other tightly, the March sisters were grateful for each other and for the chance to bond even more closely as they grew older

69
00:06:56.590 --> 00:07:03.417
together. "Well, girls, it looks as if this day is almost over," said Amy, looking up at the darkening

70
00:07:03.418 --> 00:07:08.277
sky. "A new day waits for us tomorrow," said Meg, standing up to

71
00:07:08.278 --> 00:07:16.692
leave. As Jo followed her sisters back to the house, she added, "and a new chapter in this story called

72
00:07:16.693 --> 00:07:45.534
life."

